sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Purchase API
    participant C as Closing API
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over P,D: Row selector: customer_billing_state.customer_id = C<br/>Request advisory identity: api_idempotency_operations.operation_scope<br/>plus api_idempotency_operations.idempotency_key (not a row lock)
    Note over P,D: New add-on purchase and closing both target month M.<br/>Month M has ended, and closing history permits M.
    alt Purchase gets the account first
        P->>D: BEGIN, scoped request lock, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        C->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        Note over C,D: WAIT for purchase completion
        P->>D: Check closure, snapshot addons monthly price<br/>INSERT addon_subscriptions
        Note over P,D: Purchase trigger uses the same account lock.<br/>It rejects overlapping active purchase months.
        P->>D: Advance state_version, store result, COMMIT
        D-->>C: Account lock granted
        C->>D: Include the full monthly add-on price<br/>Publish invoice and COMMIT
    else Closing gets the account first
        C->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        P->>D: BEGIN, scoped request lock<br/>FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        Note over P,D: WAIT for the invoice
        C->>D: Publish invoice without the new purchase, COMMIT
        D-->>P: Account lock granted, closure is now visible
        P->>D: ROLLBACK, return 409 billing_conflict
        Note over P,D: No retroactive subscription or request result
    end
    Note over P,D: If an older purchase wins before a later first close,<br/>closing rejects skipping its earlier active month.
